It must be recognized that although the above tasks represent general roles, each office will respond as required while respecting regional flexibility. 

The regional responsibilities may vary if a Settlement Agreement has been signed with a province.

### **6.3. Local CIC office responsibilities** 

Each region has a number of local offices delivering the programs within the provinces/territories in its region. Local responsibilities include: 

- promoting the sponsorship program with the public and community organizations; 

- assessing, approving/refusing, processing and monitoring private sponsorship undertakings; 

- registering refugees for the Interim Federal Health (IFH) Program, where required; 

- in conjunction with the visa offices, responding to representations from sponsoring groups on the status of sponsorship cases, as required; 

- delivering RAP income support and monitoring RAP clients; 

- monitoring private sponsors and privately sponsored refugees; 

- liaising with: 

   -  provinces and municipalities; 

   -  private sponsorship groups; 

