## **5.1. Humanitarian and compassionate considerations** 

The IAD has an equitable jurisdiction, which allows it to consider factors that may warrant an appeal being allowed despite the fact that the decision being appealed is valid in law. IRPA sets out the test to be applied by the IAD in order to allow a case for reasons of equity. Under IRPA, the test of equity which the IAD is to apply has been consolidated into one test for all types of appeals to the IAD by a party other than the Minister [A67(1)(c)]. When considering an appeal of a family class sponsorship, the IAD may consider some of the following factors: 

- whether the admission of the applicant would result in the reunion in Canada of the appellant with close family; 

- the strength of the relationship between the applicant and the appellant; 

